  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-149495",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let $F$ be the event that a squirrel is an adult female, $C$ be the event that a squirrel is born in captivity, and ${S}_{1},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},{S}_{4}$ be the event that a squirrel is of species $1,$ $2,$ $3,$ or $4,$ respectively. \n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- Each species has the same number of individuals, so we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({S}_{1})=P({S}_{2})=P({S}_{3})=P({S}_{4})=0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P(C|{S}_{1})=0.08 \\\\  & P(C|{S}_{2})=0.09 \\\\  & P(C|{S}_{4})=0.11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${S}_{1}⊔{S}_{2}⊔{S}_{3}⊔{S}_{4}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({S}_{1})+P({S}_{2})+P({S}_{3})+P({S}_{4})=0.25+0.25+0.25+0.25=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $42%$ of the squirrels are adult females, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.42.\n$$\n\n- Since $8%$ of adult females are born in captivity, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|F)=0.08.\n$$\n\n- Since $36%$ of squirrels born in captivity are adult females, we have\n\n$$\nP(F|C)=0.36.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen squirrel from species $3$ is born in captivity, which is represented as $P(C|{S}_{3}).$ \n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|C) & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C)} \\\\ 0.36 & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C|{S}_{1})P({S}_{1})+P(C|{S}_{2})P({S}_{2})+P(C|{S}_{3})P({S}_{3})+P(C|{S}_{4})P({S}_{4})} \\\\ 0.36 & =\\frac{(0.08)(0.42)}{(0.08)(0.25)+(0.09)(0.25)+P(C|{S}_{3})(0.25)+(0.11)(0.25)} \\\\ 0.36 & =\\frac{0.0336}{0.07+0.25P(C|{S}_{3})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $P(C|{S}_{3}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.36(0.07+0.25P(C|{S}_{3})) & =0.0336 \\\\ 0.07+0.25P(C|{S}_{3}) & =\\frac{0.0336}{0.36} \\\\ 0.07+0.25P(C|{S}_{3}) & =\\frac{7}{75} \\\\ 0.25P(C|{S}_{3}) & =\\frac{7}{75}-0.07 \\\\ P(C|{S}_{3}) & =\\frac{1}{0.25}(\\frac{7}{75}-0.07) \\\\ P(C|{S}_{3}) & ≈0.093\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.",
